<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although the main text uses the diffusion SDE formulation, we introduce the Probability Flow ODE (PF-ODE) for the proofs and for Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Generalizing DiME to arbitrary posterior marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. This ODE has identical marginals as the SDE under ideal conditions. Given diffusion process <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}=a_{t}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sigma_{t}{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\bm{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}=a_{t}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sigma_{t}{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\bm{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the PF-ODE is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d{\bm{x}}_{t}\;=\;\Big[\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\,{\bm{x}}_{t}\;-\;\left(\sigma_{t}\sigma_{t}^{\prime}-\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\Big]\,dt={\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d{\bm{x}}_{t}\;=\;\Big[\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\,{\bm{x}}_{t}\;-\;\left(\sigma_{t}\sigma_{t}^{\prime}-\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\Big]\,dt={\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the unconditional flow. The conditional flow <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> can be derived via Bayes:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\,{\bm{x}}_{t}\;-\;\left(\sigma_{t}\sigma_{t}^{\prime}-\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\,{\bm{x}}_{t}\;-\;\left(\sigma_{t}\sigma_{t}^{\prime}-\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})-\left(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\right)\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})-\left(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\right)\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For the following proof, we impose the regularity and smoothness assumptions listed in Appendix A of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al. (2021a)</a></cite> for both the prior marginals <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and the posterior marginals <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be the unconditional diffusion marginal and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be a posterior time-marginal obtained at diffusion timestep <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> as their corresponding velocity vector fields.
We have the following identity:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\left({\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\right)^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\left({\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\right)^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Simplifying the derivative gives:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\left[\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\left[\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Product rule)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we expand the first term. Let <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> be the flows at <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> respectively:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\int\left[\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\int\left[\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\int\nabla\cdot(\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}))\big[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\big]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\int\nabla\cdot(\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}))\big[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\big]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Continuity equation)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phantom{-}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\big[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\big]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phantom{-}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\big[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\big]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Integration by parts)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phantom{-}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phantom{-}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Bayes)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second term:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]-\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]-\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phantom{-}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\left[\nabla\cdot{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})+{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phantom{-}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\left[\nabla\cdot{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})+{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex11.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Log-continuity equation)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phantom{-}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\left[\nabla\cdot{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})+{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phantom{-}\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\left[\nabla\cdot{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})+{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\phantom{=}-\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phantom{=}-\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex13.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Bayes)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}}){\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex14.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Stein’s identity)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Adding the two terms back together gives us:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\left({\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\right)^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\left({\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\right)^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\left({\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\right)^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\left({\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\right)^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (DiME: Model evidence estimation along the standard marginals). ‣ 3 Estimating the model evidence along the standard marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding out the KL divergence gives us an expression for the model evidence:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\big[\log p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{0})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\big[\log p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})-\log p({\bm{x}}_{0})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\big[\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})-\log p({\bm{y}})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\big[\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})-\log p({\bm{y}})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\!\big[\,\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big]-\log p({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\!\big[\,\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big]-\log p({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies\log p({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies\log p({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\!\big[\,\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big]-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{0}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\!\big[\,\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big]-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{0})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">At the final diffusion step, the forward process has destroyed all information about the measurements, so we have <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})=p({\bm{x}}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})=p({\bm{x}}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{T}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{T}))=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int_{0}^{T}\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{t}))dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int_{0}^{T}\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{t}))dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{=}\;-\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\Big[\big({\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\big)^{\!\top}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\Big]\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0.280em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(i)}{=}\;-\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\Big[\big({\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\big)^{\!\top}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\Big]\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(ii)}{=}\;\int_{0}^{T}\Big(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\tfrac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\Big)\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\big\|\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\big\|^{2}\,dt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(ii)}{=}\;\int_{0}^{T}\Big(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\tfrac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}\Big)\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\big\|\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\big\|^{2}\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\left(\sigma_{t_{i}}^{\prime}\sigma_{t_{i}}-\sigma_{t_{i}}^{2}\frac{a_{t_{i}}^{\prime}}{a_{t_{i}}}\right)\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\|\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\left(\sigma_{t_{i}}^{\prime}\sigma_{t_{i}}-\sigma_{t_{i}}^{2}\frac{a_{t_{i}}^{\prime}}{a_{t_{i}}}\right)\mathop{\mathbb{E}}\limits_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\|\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where (i) uses Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> but with <math id="A1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})=p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})=p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> and (ii) uses the PF-ODE of the conditional flow (Eq. <a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proofs and derivations for the DAPS-based implementation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 3.1 An improved approximation for the posterior covariance ‣ 3 Estimating the model evidence along the standard marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our diffusion corruption process gives us:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a_{t}^{2}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}+\sigma_{t}^{2}{\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a_{t}^{2}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}+\sigma_{t}^{2}{\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0},a_{t}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sigma_{t}{\bm{z}}_{t})=a_{t}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0})=a_{t}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0},a_{t}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sigma_{t}{\bm{z}}_{t})=a_{t}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0})=a_{t}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging these into the Gaussian posterior covariance formula gives:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0})-\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{t})\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{-1}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0})-\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{t})\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{-1}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\Sigma}_{0}-a_{t}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}\left[a_{t}^{2}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}+\sigma_{t}^{2}{\bm{I}}\right]^{-1}a_{t}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\Sigma}_{0}-a_{t}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}\left[a_{t}^{2}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}+\sigma_{t}^{2}{\bm{I}}\right]^{-1}a_{t}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\Sigma}_{0}-\bm{\Sigma}_{0}\left[\bm{\Sigma}_{0}+\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{a_{t}^{2}}{\bm{I}}\right]^{-1}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\Sigma}_{0}-\bm{\Sigma}_{0}\left[\bm{\Sigma}_{0}+\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{a_{t}^{2}}{\bm{I}}\right]^{-1}\bm{\Sigma}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\bm{\Sigma}_{0}^{-1}+\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\bm{I}}\right]^{-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\bm{\Sigma}_{0}^{-1}+\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\bm{I}}\right]^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hfill\text{(Woodbury identity)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>(Woodbury identity)</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hfill\text{(Woodbury identity)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the training data has <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{max}}(\bm{\Sigma}_{0})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{max}}(\bm{\Sigma}_{0})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\|=\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\|=\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging in the covariance from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 3.1 An improved approximation for the posterior covariance ‣ 3 Estimating the model evidence along the standard marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> gives:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{\text{max}}\left[\bm{\Sigma}_{0}^{-1}+\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\bm{I}}\right]^{-1}=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\text{min}}\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{0}^{-1}+\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\bm{I}}\right)}=\frac{1}{1+\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}}=\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{\text{max}}\left[\bm{\Sigma}_{0}^{-1}+\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\bm{I}}\right]^{-1}=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\text{min}}\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{0}^{-1}+\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\bm{I}}\right)}=\frac{1}{1+\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}}=\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 3.2 Estimating the squared likelihood score ‣ 3 Estimating the model evidence along the standard marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Tweedie’s rule, we can show that <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{high}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{high}</annotation></semantics></math> is unbiased for the likelihood score:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\!\left(\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]-\frac{{\bm{x}}_{t}}{a_{t}}\right)-\frac{a_{t}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\!\left(\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}]-\frac{{\bm{x}}_{t}}{a_{t}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\!\left(\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]-\frac{{\bm{x}}_{t}}{a_{t}}\right)-\frac{a_{t}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\!\left(\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}]-\frac{{\bm{x}}_{t}}{a_{t}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left(\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]-\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left(\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]-\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋆</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our Gaussian approximation of <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> gives us <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})=-\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}^{-1}({\bm{x}}_{0}-\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})=-\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}^{-1}({\bm{x}}_{0}-\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}])</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the fact that the expectation of the score is zero, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}+\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}+\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}+\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\left(\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})+\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\right)\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}+\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\left(\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})+\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\right)\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}-({\bm{x}}_{0}-\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}])+\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}-({\bm{x}}_{0}-\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}])+\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}]+\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})}[\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}]+\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})}[\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⋆</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star\star</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\star\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star\star)</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math> shows that <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{low}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{low}</annotation></semantics></math> is unbiased.
To compute a variance bound for <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{high}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{high}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\Theta_{high})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\Theta_{high})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex40.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Gaussian conditional covariance)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}(\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}(\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex41.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Corollary <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1. ‣ A.1 Proofs and derivations for the DAPS-based implementation ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The term <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is of constant order over the diffusion process, resulting in a variance of <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}^{2}/\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}^{2}/\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. To compute a bound for <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{low}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{low}</annotation></semantics></math>, we linearize the likelihood <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> at a fixed <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}=\left.\frac{\partial f}{\partial{\bm{x}}}\right|_{\bar{{\bm{x}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}=\left.\frac{\partial f}{\partial{\bm{x}}}\right|_{\bar{{\bm{x}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and get</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\Theta_{low})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\Theta_{low})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\mathrm{Cov}(\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\mathrm{Cov}(\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\mathrm{Cov}(\frac{1}{\sigma_{\bm{y}}^{2}}{\bm{A}}^{T}({\bm{y}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}\mathrm{Cov}(\frac{1}{\sigma_{\bm{y}}^{2}}{\bm{A}}^{T}({\bm{y}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\bm{y}}^{4}}\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}{\bm{A}}^{T}{\bm{A}}\left(\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})\right){\bm{A}}^{T}{\bm{A}}\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\bm{y}}^{4}}\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}{\bm{A}}^{T}{\bm{A}}\left(\frac{a_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{4}}\mathrm{Cov}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})\right){\bm{A}}^{T}{\bm{A}}\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\|{\bm{A}}\|^{4}}{\sigma_{\bm{y}}^{4}}\frac{\sigma_{t}^{4}}{(\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2})^{2}}\mathrm{Var}(\Theta_{high})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\|{\bm{A}}\|^{4}}{\sigma_{\bm{y}}^{4}}\frac{\sigma_{t}^{4}}{(\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2})^{2}}\mathrm{Var}(\Theta_{high}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex45.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Corollary <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1. ‣ A.1 Proofs and derivations for the DAPS-based implementation ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\|{\bm{A}}\|^{4}}{\sigma_{\bm{y}}^{4}}\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}a_{t}^{2}}{(\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2})^{3}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\|{\bm{A}}\|^{4}}{\sigma_{\bm{y}}^{4}}\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}a_{t}^{2}}{(\sigma_{t}^{2}+a_{t}^{2})^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Unlike <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{high}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{high}</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance of this estimator goes to <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, but for the rest of diffusion process the constant factor makes it a higher variance estimator than <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{high}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{high}</annotation></semantics></math> in practice.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Generalizing <span id="A2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME</span> to arbitrary posterior marginals</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While we only present <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME</span> along the standard marginals in the main text, <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME</span> can be extended to any arbitrary diffusion posterior marginals that anneal to the true posterior as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 2</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Generalized <span id="Thmcorollary2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME</span>)<span id="Thmcorollary2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmcorollary2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be the unconditional diffusion marginal and <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be a path of marginals that anneals to the true posterior, or <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})=p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})=p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> as their corresponding velocity fields. Given reverse diffusion timesteps <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=t_{0}&lt;\dots&lt;t_{N}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=t_{0}&lt;\dots&lt;t_{N}=T</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\!\big[\,\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big]-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})}\!\big[\,\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\,\big]-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\approx-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\Big[\big({\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\big)^{\!\top}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≈</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\Big[\big({\bm{v}}_{\pi}({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})-{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})\big)^{\!\top}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{T}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{T})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Follows directly from the proof of Prop. <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (DiME: Model evidence estimation along the standard marginals). ‣ 3 Estimating the model evidence along the standard marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">While <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> can be directly computed using the PF-ODE (Eq. <a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), computing <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> can be difficult for arbitrary time-marginals <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. By crafting a sequence of diffusion marginals with known velocity, we can avoid any approximation like the one used for <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in the DAPS implementation. The marginals <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> should also ideally have high overlap with the unconditional marginal <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure accurate computation of <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> when the score is learned.
If <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})\neq p({\bm{x}}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})\neq p({\bm{x}}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, then we must use other estimation methods to compute <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{T}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})||p({\bm{x}}_{T}))</annotation></semantics></math> or settle for an unnormalized model evidence estimate. The following section discusses two estimators that does not require any approximation, but are not normalized.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Estimating the model evidence from alternative sampling methods</h3>

<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> One posterior sample-path of <span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME-PnPDM</span> </figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Score-based model <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, measurement <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, noise schedule <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{i})_{i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{i})_{i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}}</annotation></semantics></math>,

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             Sample <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;"> Initialize the integral sum, <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=N,N-1\ldots,0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=N,N-1\ldots,0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0})\propto q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})p({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0})\propto q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})p({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;"> Update the integral sum <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\leftarrow f-(t_{i}-t_{i-1}){\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒗</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">i</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">∇</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">i</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\leftarrow f-(t_{i}-t_{i-1}){\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math></span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The PnP-DM marginals follow <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\propto q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\propto q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a time-independent likelihood term. As a result, the initial distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})\neq p({\bm{x}}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})\neq p({\bm{x}}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> and the KL divergence <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{T}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{y}})\|p({\bm{x}}_{T}))</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero, so we can only compute the unnormalized model evidence.
However, the unknown constant is dependent on <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the forward model, so this unnormalized quantity can still be used for model selection.
We derive the estimator in Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (DiME-PnPDM: model evidence estimation along the PnP-DM marginals). ‣ B.1 Estimating the model evidence from alternative sampling methods ‣ Appendix B Generalizing DiME to arbitrary posterior marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and implement it with PnP-DM in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ B.1 Estimating the model evidence from alternative sampling methods ‣ Appendix B Generalizing DiME to arbitrary posterior marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME-PnPDM</span>: model evidence estimation along the PnP-DM marginals)<span id="Thmproposition2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given diffusion process <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}=a_{t}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sigma_{t}{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\bm{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}=a_{t}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sigma_{t}{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\bm{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>, PnP-DM marginals <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and timesteps <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=t_{0}&lt;\dots&lt;t_{N}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=t_{0}&lt;\dots&lt;t_{N}=T</annotation></semantics></math>, the model evidence can be estimated via:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})\approx C(q,{\bm{y}})-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})\approx C(q,{\bm{y}})-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q,{\bm{y}})=\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\bm{I}})}\left[q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q,{\bm{y}})=\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\bm{I}})}\left[q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is constant for fixed measurement <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and forward model, and <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})=\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{t}-(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}})\nabla_{\bm{x}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})=\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{t}-(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}})\nabla_{\bm{x}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the PF-ODE velocity at <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">While we can apply Corollary <a href="#Thmcorollary2" title="Corollary 2 (Generalized DiME). ‣ Appendix B Generalizing DiME to arbitrary posterior marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we can take a shortcut to cancel some extra terms. Under the PnP-DM marginals, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t)</annotation></semantics></math> is time-dependent while the likelihood <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is time-independent, so we can directly compute the derivative of the evidence:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex50.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Fisher’s identity)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\nabla\cdot{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})+{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\nabla\cdot{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})+{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex51.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Log-cont. equation)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\nabla\cdot{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})+{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[\nabla\cdot{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})+{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex53.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Bayes)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex54.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(Stein’s identity)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating over all <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> gives us the estimator:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t=0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)-\int_{0}^{T}\frac{d}{dt}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)-\int_{0}^{T}\frac{d}{dt}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)=\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{T}^{2})}\left[q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)=\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{T}^{2})}\left[q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is the model evidence under a Gaussian prior, and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})=\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{t}-(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}})\nabla_{\bm{x}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})=\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{t}-(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}})\nabla_{\bm{x}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the PF-ODE from Equation <a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We can also do a similar derivation for the marginals used for the Twisted Diffusion Sampler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, which follow <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}|{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})p({\bm{y}}|\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}|{\bm{x}}_{t}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}|{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})p({\bm{y}}|\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}|{\bm{x}}_{t}])</annotation></semantics></math>; note that this evidence gradient can be computed before resampling using SMC weights or after resampling without weights.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME-TDS</span>: model evidence estimation along the TDS marginals)<span id="Thmproposition3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given diffusion process <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}=a_{t}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sigma_{t}{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\bm{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}=a_{t}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sigma_{t}{\bm{z}}_{t},{\bm{z}}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\bm{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>, TDS marginals <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}|{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝛍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}|{\bm{y}})\propto p({\bm{x}}_{t})p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>, and timesteps <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=t_{0}&lt;\dots&lt;t_{N}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=t_{0}&lt;\dots&lt;t_{N}=T</annotation></semantics></math>, the model evidence can be estimated via:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})\approx C(q,{\bm{y}})-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}))+\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})\approx C(q,{\bm{y}})-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}))+\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q,{\bm{y}})=\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{T}^{2})}\left[p({\bm{y}}\mid\mu({\bm{x}}_{T}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q,{\bm{y}})=\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{T}^{2})}\left[p({\bm{y}}\mid\mu({\bm{x}}_{T}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is constant for fixed measurement <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and forward model, and <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})=\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{t}-(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}})\nabla_{\bm{x}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})=\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{t}-(\sigma_{t}^{\prime}\sigma_{t}-\sigma_{t}^{2}\frac{a_{t}^{\prime}}{a_{t}})\nabla_{\bm{x}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the PF-ODE velocity at <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)}\frac{d}{dt}\int p({\bm{x}}_{t})p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)}\frac{d}{dt}\int p({\bm{x}}_{t})p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)}\int\left[\frac{d}{dt}p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))d{\bm{x}}_{t}+\frac{1}{\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)}\int p({\bm{x}}_{t})\left[\frac{d}{dt}p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)}\int\left[\frac{d}{dt}p({\bm{x}}_{t})\right]p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))d{\bm{x}}_{t}+\frac{1}{\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)}\int p({\bm{x}}_{t})\left[\frac{d}{dt}p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))\right]d{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid y)}\left[\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})+\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid y)}\left[\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})+\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))+\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))+\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line is derived in a similarly to Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (DiME-PnPDM: model evidence estimation along the PnP-DM marginals). ‣ B.1 Estimating the model evidence from alternative sampling methods ‣ Appendix B Generalizing DiME to arbitrary posterior marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Integrating over all <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> gives the estimator:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)-\int_{0}^{T}\frac{d}{dt}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)-\int_{0}^{T}\frac{d}{dt}\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}))+\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid t=T)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Delta t_{i}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{t}\sim\pi({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}\mid{\bm{y}})}\left[{\bm{v}}_{p}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}})^{T}\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}))+\frac{d}{dt}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{\mu}}({\bm{x}}_{t_{i}}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid T)\approx\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{T}^{2})}\left[p({\bm{y}}\mid\mu({\bm{x}}_{T}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi({\bm{y}}\mid T)\approx\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{T}^{2})}\left[p({\bm{y}}\mid\mu({\bm{x}}_{T}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Baseline methods</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Benchmarking on Gaussian Mixture Prior with Ground Truth Evidence ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we compared to five baseline methods, described here. Define <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> as an intermediate distribution of the <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">power-posterior path</span>, used in TI, AIS, and SMC: <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}({\bm{x}})\propto p({\bm{x}})p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\beta},\beta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}({\bm{x}})\propto p({\bm{x}})p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\beta},\beta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that this path is equivalent to the <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">geometric path</span>
under a different parametrization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Naive Monte Carlo (Naive MC)</span>: We generate many unconditional prior samples and compute the expectation of the likelihood as follows: <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p({\bm{y}})=\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0})}[p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p({\bm{y}})=\log\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0})}[p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Original DAPS covariance heuristic (Original heuristic)</span>: We perform the same steps as described in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 Estimating the squared likelihood score ‣ 3 Estimating the model evidence along the standard marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> but using the originally proposed covariance heuristic <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}=\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}}=\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Thermodynamic integration (TI)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lartillot and Philippe, 2006</a>)</cite>: Originally from statistical mechanics, TI can also compute expectations by integrating the evidence over the power-posterior path:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\beta}\log p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\beta}\log p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})}\frac{d}{d\beta}p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})}\int p({\bm{x}})\frac{d}{d\beta}p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\beta}d{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})}\frac{d}{d\beta}p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})}\int p({\bm{x}})\frac{d}{d\beta}p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\beta}d{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})}\int p({\bm{x}})p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\beta}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})d{\bm{x}}=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p_{\beta}}[\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{p_{\beta}({\bm{y}})}\int p({\bm{x}})p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\beta}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})d{\bm{x}}=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p_{\beta}}[\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Using the fact that <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\beta=0}({\bm{y}})=\log 1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\beta=0}({\bm{y}})=\log 1=0</annotation></semantics></math>, using <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> integration steps we have the estimator:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{\beta=1}({\bm{y}})\;\approx\;\sum_{k=1}^{K}\Delta\beta_{k}\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p_{\beta_{k-1}}}\!\left[\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{\beta=1}({\bm{y}})\;\approx\;\sum_{k=1}^{K}\Delta\beta_{k}\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p_{\beta_{k-1}}}\!\left[\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Samples from each <math id="A3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> were generated using Sequential Monte Carlo (details below).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Annealed importance sampling (AIS)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Neal, 2001</a>)</cite>: We can compute the ratio of evidence:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{p_{\beta_{k}}({\bm{y}})}{p_{\beta_{k-1}}({\bm{y}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{p_{\beta_{k}}({\bm{y}})}{p_{\beta_{k-1}}({\bm{y}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\int p({\bm{x}})p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\beta_{k-1}}p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\Delta\beta_{k}}d{\bm{x}}}{p_{\beta_{k-1}}({\bm{y}})}=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p_{\beta_{k-1}}}[p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\Delta\beta_{k}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\int p({\bm{x}})p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\beta_{k-1}}p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\Delta\beta_{k}}d{\bm{x}}}{p_{\beta_{k-1}}({\bm{y}})}=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p_{\beta_{k-1}}}[p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}})^{\Delta\beta_{k}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p_{{\bm{x}}\sim\beta_{k-1}}}[\exp(\Delta\beta_{k}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}))]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{p_{{\bm{x}}\sim\beta_{k-1}}}[\exp(\Delta\beta_{k}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}))].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Using the fact that <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\beta=0}({\bm{y}})=\log 1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\beta=0}({\bm{y}})=\log 1=0</annotation></semantics></math>, telescoping over all <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\beta=1}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\beta=1}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{p_{\beta_{k-1}}}[\exp(\Delta\beta_{k}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{p_{\beta_{k-1}}}[\exp(\Delta\beta_{k}\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0:k-1}\sim p_{\beta_{0:k-1}}}\exp\!\Big(\sum_{k=1}^{K}\Delta\beta_{k}\,\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{k-1})\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0:k-1}\sim p_{\beta_{0:k-1}}}\exp\!\Big(\sum_{k=1}^{K}\Delta\beta_{k}\,\log p({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{x}}_{k-1})\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0:k-1}\sim p_{\beta_{0:k-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0:k-1}\sim p_{\beta_{0:k-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the sample-path of one particle, where each transition kernel from <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> was performed using Langevin dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sequential Monte Carlo (SMC)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Del Moral et al., 2006</a>)</cite>: An extension of AIS that uses the resampling step from Sequential Monte Carlo methods to replace particles with degenerate weights (i.e. particles stuck in the wrong mode) while sampling the next intermediate distribution, potentially reducing both bias and variance. These resampling steps are performed either using a fixed schedule or adaptively when the effective sample size falls below a threshold.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Implementation details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span><span id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME</span></h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DiME</span> is implemented alongside DAPS, we have a similar set of hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Number of diffusion steps for sampling <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></span>:
While the original DAPS method uses many diffusion steps to estimate the denoised image at each annealing iteration, we use 1 diffusion step to ensure an exact estimate of <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[{\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math> by Tweedie’s formula.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Langevin dynamics</span>: The learning rate of Langevin dynamics was tuned so that posterior samples <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{0}\sim p({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> have a mean reduced <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> data likelihood fit that converges as low as possible (ideally around 1, which is indicative of a good posterior sample for likelihoods with Gaussian noise). We also use a linear learning rate decay as is done in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025)</a></cite>. The table below lists the learning rates and maximum step counts used for each experiment. In practice, sample convergence usually happens much sooner than the maximum step count.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.SS1.tab1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.SS1.tab1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Task</td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lr</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Max steps</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Mixture of Gaussians (in-distribution)</td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.SS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{,}000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Mixture of Gaussians (out-of-distribution)</td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.SS1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.SS1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Mixture of Gaussians (saddle point)</td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.SS1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.SS1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Fourier phase retrieval</td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.SS1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.SS1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Gaussian phase retrieval</td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.SS1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.SS1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">M87* black hole imaging</td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.SS1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.tab1.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.SS1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Selection of <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{min}</annotation></semantics></math></span>: This parameter can be viewed as the minimum noise level that the learned score can still be trusted. For the analytic Mixture of Gaussians experiment, we use a minimum annealing noise level <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{min}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{min}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, and for the diffusion model experiments, we use <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{min}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{min}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> as is done in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
The remaining integral from <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=t_{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=t_{min}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 1 (DiME: Model evidence estimation along the standard marginals). ‣ 3 Estimating the model evidence along the standard marginals ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> is approximated by a trapezoid, using the fact that the integrand equals <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Computing the precision matrix <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{0}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{0}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></span>: for some datasets, the covariance of specific pixel locations is nearly 0 (such as the corner regions of MNIST), so we added a jitter of 1e-2 for stability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Baselines</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use TI, AIS, and SMC as baseline methods for the mixture of Gaussians experiment (Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Benchmarking on Gaussian Mixture Prior with Ground Truth Evidence ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) and SMC for the MNIST experiment (Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Model Selection Using Learned Score on Non-convex Inverse Problems ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>; Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Baseline results on MNIST Model Selection ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>). We used Langevin dynamics with 2000 steps and learning rate 0.0002 for our transitions between distributions. For SMC, we resample when the effective sample size (ESS) is less than 0.6.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We test with fixed linear, exponential, sigmoidal <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> as well as adaptive <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> schedules that decrease the Conditional ESS at a constant rate of [0.5, 0.6, 0.7]. For the mixture of Gaussians study, an exponential schedule with <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=6</annotation></semantics></math> was found to be optimal. For the MNIST experiment, the fixed schedules use 50 annealing steps, while the adaptive schedule had a minimum <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> step size of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.002" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.002</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.002</annotation></semantics></math> which in practice results in <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>150</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">150</annotation></semantics></math> steps at most.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Baseline results on MNIST Model Selection</h2>

<figure id="A5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20549v1/figures/phase_retrieval_baseline.png" id="A5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:466/242;" width="466" height="242" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Model evidence confusion matrix using sequential Monte Carlo (SMC) for Gaussian phase retrieval (<span id="A5.F6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">left</span>) and Fourier phase retrieval (<span id="A5.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">right</span>) for each (ground truth measurement, model) pair of MNIST digits. When SMC uses the learned diffusion score <math id="A5.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{x}}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{x}}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A5.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> as the prior score, it often fails to select the correct model.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Results of the MNIST experiment (Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Model Selection Using Learned Score on Non-convex Inverse Problems ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) using SMC and the learned <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{x}}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{x}}}\log p({\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> as a prior score are shown in Figure <a href="#A5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix E Baseline results on MNIST Model Selection ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. SMC is often unable to determine the correct MNIST model.
Each SMC annealing step also takes about <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="10\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\times</annotation></semantics></math> longer than an equivalent annealing step for <span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">DiME</span>, due to having to query the diffusion model many times for the prior score. Interestingly, narrower priors (i.e. MNIST digit 1) leads to <span id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">higher</span> model evidence estimates here; since the training data is more clumped together, the learned score becomes more accurate at low noise levels.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, the model evidence estimates of a few runs over all temperature annealing schedules as well as for a second noise level, <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, are reported in Tables <a href="#A5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Appendix E Baseline results on MNIST Model Selection ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#A5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix E Baseline results on MNIST Model Selection ‣ Sample-efficient evidence estimation of score based priors for model selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Mean and standard deviation over 5 runs is shown here. As can be seen, lowering the noise level only further increases overfitting to training data, causing the estimated evidence to drop.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
